      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Types of Protected Areas in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Protected areas in India are structured into National Parks, Wildlife Sanctuaries, and Biosphere Reserves.",
        "Major Tiger Reserves represent targeted species protection and habitat conservation initiatives across Indian states.",
        "Government Wildlife Conservation Programs establish the regulatory framework and active schemes for protecting endangered species.",
        "Understanding the importance of wildlife conservation is essential for ecological balance and biodiversity management."
      ],
      "id": "ex5wpor"
    },
